drm/virtio: an overlay plane on each CRTC when virtio_gpu.overlay_plane=1

LG's O22N2 sets (W24G spacebuns) have one TV connector and one CRTC with a
primary, an overlay and a cursor plane (lg1kdrm, use_overlay on by default).
Their Weston frontend writes a second output section (TV-2, the popup window)
from the configuration, the drm-backend copies the connector into a second
head for it, and that output takes the CRTC's overlay plane when the primary
is in use. Without an overlay plane TV-2 is never enabled, LSMW's secondary
window never gets its controllers, and the compositor faults in
getFocusedWindowInfo.

With the parameter set, each CRTC gets an overlay plane with the primary's
formats that may be positioned and clipped. A virtio scanout shows one
resource and composes nothing, so the overlay is scanned out only while the
primary plane has no framebuffer (LG's exclusive output path turns TV-1's
primary off and shows TV-2's buffer): the scanout then shows the overlay's
visible source rectangle at its own size; its position on the CRTC is not
kept. With the primary on, the overlay is accepted but not shown. Unset,
nothing changes.

